# gpu_capture native addon — the BUILT artifact stays tracked, its scratch does not.
# Keeping gpu_capture.node in git is deliberate: CI never runs `npm run build:native` (ci.yml does
# `npm ci`, whose prepare script is tsc-only), so on macos-latest the committed binary is the only
# thing loadGpuCapture() can find. Drop it and the suite silently degrades from `shared` capture to
# `direct` — green either way, which is precisely the failure this repo tries not to ship. Rebuild
# it with `npm run build:native` after any Electron major bump (it is ABI-pinned; 43.x = ABI 148).
# Everything else under build/ is node-gyp / @electron/rebuild scratch — Makefiles, config.gypi,
# .deps and .o files — that bakes in an absolute path to whatever worktree last built it, so it
# churns every diff and is regenerable in one command. bin/ is @electron/rebuild's per-ABI cache.
src/render/native/electron/native/build/*
!src/render/native/electron/native/build/Release/
src/render/native/electron/native/build/Release/*
!src/render/native/electron/native/build/Release/gpu_capture.node
src/render/native/electron/native/bin/
